        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2003",
        "question_text": "<p>Which of the following is a characteristic feature of <b>hardwood</b> as opposed to softwood?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Hardwoods are typically derived from <i>deciduous trees</i> and have broad leaves. They are generally denser, harder, and more durable than softwoods, which come from <i>coniferous trees</i>. Hardwoods also have vessels (pores) in their structure, which softwoods lack.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
